{"updated_at": {"date": {"d": "10", "m": "08", "Y": "2026"}, "time": {"H": "09", "M": "04", "S": "39"}}, "news": [{"title": "Indore: 8.5% rise in property registrations in last four months", "para": "Indore's real estate market has witnessed a thriving boost, with property transactions rising by 8.5 percent, generating significant revenue for the state. The expansion of outer corridors and emerging zones is driving this surge. Interestingly, property sales in older, central regions are experiencing a slight downturn. Overall, this trend highlights a strong rebound in the local property sector.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/residential/indore-8-5-rise-in-property-registrations-in-last-four-months/133088554?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-104236/133088554.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "residential"}, {"title": "Nagpur: 88% of buildings lack OCs, union minister sets four-month deadline to resolve issue", "para": "Nearly eighty-eight percent of Nagpur's buildings lack mandatory Occupancy Certificates. Union minister Nitin Gadkari directed notices for pending issues within four months. Registrations of independent houses will continue under existing legal rules. Confusion arose over building permission certificates and Occupancy Certificates for large buildings. Developers failing to obtain Occupancy Certificates will not be allowed property registration.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/industry/nagpur-88-of-buildings-lack-ocs-union-minister-sets-four-month-deadline-to-resolve-issue/133088420?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-136712/133088420.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "industry"}, {"title": "Bihar government eyes digitisation of five crore land and property records", "para": "Bihar is undertaking a monumental task by digitizing nearly five crore land registration records dating back to 1908. This innovative initiative aims to ensure that property documents are not only secure but also easily accessible online for citizens. While records from 1996 onward have been successfully digitized and verified, the department's current focus is on the older documents from the 1990-95 period.", "href": "https://realty.economictimes.indiatimes.com/news/technology/bihar-government-eyes-digitisation-of-five-crore-land-and-property-records/133081350?utm_source=newslisting&utm_medium=latestNews", "img": "data:image/png;base64, ", "img-src": "https://etimg.etb2bimg.com/thumb/img-size-102400/133081350.cms?width=150&height=112", "tag": "technology"}]}